# function target() { return this }  target.call(self);  new Proxy(target, {})();  function other() { return this }  other.call(self);  new Proxy(other, {}).call(self)
# A call that names no receiver hands undefined on as `this`, also where a proxy without an `apply` trap stands between the call and the function. A call through a proxy that names a receiver hands that one on and nothing else.
